    .map(Files::readString)    ← IOException not allowed!
    .toList()

  Fix with try-catch wrapper:

  paths.stream()
    .map(path -> {
        try {
            return Files.readString(path);   ← checked exception
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new UncheckedIOException(e); ← wrap in unchecked
        }
    })
    .toList()
```
